WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:38.329
All politics is tribal. 

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:40.373
We're not arguing over policies, really.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:42.042
We're arguing over team colors. 

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.586
It's one reason why
 things are going to become so disastrous.

00:00:44.669 --> 00:00:47.088
And so what you need to do is
 you need to try to

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:50.550
introduce
 a different dynamic of tribalism.

00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:54.471
I have a clear vision for what
 the forward party can become.

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:56.765
And I'm really excited about it. 

00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:59.517
It's this unifying 

00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:03.688
tribe
 that's positive and uplifting in politics

00:01:03.688 --> 00:01:06.733
that a lot of people
 have been waiting for. 

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:25.043
Hey, everybody. 

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:26.336
Welcome to the podcast. 

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:30.882
My guest today is Andrew Yang,
 who is arguably one of,

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:34.803
if not the most original thinkers
 on the political scene,

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:39.974
