in terms of the psychological differences
 between Democrats and Republicans.

00:12:43.846 --> 00:12:46.140
So can you elucidate that a little bit?

00:12:46.265 --> 00:12:46.432
Yeah. 

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:51.771
Jonathan is such an incredible
 philosopher, really.

00:12:52.104 --> 00:12:54.482
He's a friend as well. 

00:12:54.482 --> 00:12:56.358
And his work on

00:12:57.359 --> 00:12:59.069
the righteous mind, how 

00:12:59.069 --> 00:13:03.449
Americans can disagree on politics
 while still being good people,

00:13:03.783 --> 00:13:07.161
I think is one of the most important works
 of our time.

00:13:07.787 --> 00:13:11.207
So he makes the case that there are six
 universal values

00:13:11.207 --> 00:13:13.584
in human culture that transcend

00:13:14.668 --> 00:13:16.045
national borders. 

00:13:16.045 --> 00:13:19.965
They are caring, fairness, liberty,

00:13:20.508 --> 00:13:23.677
loyalty authority and sanctity.

00:13:24.011 --> 00:13:27.681
And it turns out that Democrats and
 Republicans respond to different values.

00:13:28.516 --> 00:13:30.684
And that list 

00:13:30.684 --> 00:13:33.354
Democrats tend to respond
 more to caring and fairness.

00:13:33.687 --> 00:13:35.272
And Republicans tend to respond 

00:13:35.272 --> 00:13:37.691
and respond
 more to loyalty, authority and sanctity.

00:13:37.691 --> 00:13:39.819
And then the two sides
 define liberty differently.

00:13:40.486 --> 00:13:43.697
And so what you see is you have news
 media organizations that really hammered

00:13:43.697 --> 00:13:46.951
different themes that strike that chord
